= The Death of Hermann Sarrow

@pm
on-arrival: muller_died_in_office = 1

Chancellor Hermann Sarrow has died while in office. He will be greatly missed. But now, we must select a new Chancellor.

- @braun_chancellor: Otto Bristol (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>) for Chancellor.
- @wels_chancellor: Otto Vesh (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>) for Chancellor.
- @breitscheid_chancellor: Rudolf Yardley (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>) for Chancellor.
- @bruning_chancellor: Let Heinrich Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] become Chancellor.
- @wirth_chancellor: Joseph Werth of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] should be Chancellor.

@braun_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Bristol"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; unionist_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; unionist_relation -= 3 if heartland_leader == "Bristol"; gold_relation -= 3 if heartland_leader == "Bristol"; ddp_relation -= 3 if heartland_leader == "Bristol"; lvp_relation -= 3 if heartland_leader == "Bristol"
subtitle: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is worried about having so much power in one man.

Our coalition partners are reluctant to accept the new Chancellor, but they do not make loud objections.


@wels_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Vesh"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; unionist_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3
subtitle: He is a good organizer, but is he also a good chancellor?

Our coalition partners are reluctant to accept the new Chancellor, but they do not make loud objections.

@breitscheid_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Yardley"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; unionist_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; collectivist_relation += 3
subtitle: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is worried about his left-leaning tendencies.

Our coalition partners are reluctant to accept the new Chancellor, but they do not make loud objections.

@bruning_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; unionist_relation += 5; gold_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5; coalition_dissent -= 1; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion += 1; lvp_left += 1
subtitle: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] claims it is their turn...

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is grateful that we have supported Askew for Chancellor.

@wirth_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Werth"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; unionist_relation += 5; gold_relation += 2; ddp_relation += 2; lvp_relation += 2
view-if: unionist_ideology == "Left"
subtitle: As a moderate member of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], he could represent unity.

Our coalition partners accept Joseph Werth of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] as the new Chancellor.


@not_pm

Hermann Sarrow, one of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>'s long-time leaders, has died. He will be greatly missed.
